# Open record parameter accepts closed record argument
# Function f expects an open record [x: Int ...] — any record with at least x: Int.
# We call it with a closed record [x: 42] (no extra fields).
# This should work: closed records are subtypes of open records with the same base fields.
[f: [fn [let r@[x: Int ...]] r.x]
 result: [f [x: 42]]]
=== out
Dict({"f": Function(r), "result": Int(42)})
